      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "To better understand the historical roots of MCMC, we digress for a moment to discuss the original Monte Carlo approach, which used random-number generation to approximate integrals. Suppose we wish to compute a complex integral, $$ \\int_{a}^{b}h(x)dx $$",
      "source_page": 1208,
